/* FamilyOS Launcher stylesheet.

Confirmed via a real QEMU boot test: no stylesheet was ever loaded
anywhere in this codebase, so the launcher rendered as plain default-Qt
buttons on a flat white/gray background - none of graphics/'s branding
work was actually reaching the screen, and app-grid buttons sized
themselves individually off their own text/icon content (GCompris's
button visibly smaller than the others).

Colors are the project's own already-established palette, sampled
directly from graphics/branding/familyos-logo.svg (#2E7D32 deep green,
#F9A825 amber, #FFFFFF) rather than invented here - same flat,
bold-outline, high-contrast visual language docs/Asset_Sourcing.md
describes borrowing from sugar-artwork for kid-facing UI.
*/

QMainWindow, QDialog {
    background-color: #FFF8E1;
}

QPushButton#appCard {
    background-color: #2E7D32;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 24px;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: bold;
    min-width: 140px;
    min-height: 100px;
    max-height: 240px;
    padding: 10px;
}

QPushButton#appCard:pressed {
    background-color: #245e27;
}

QToolButton#parentAnchor {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    min-width: 28px;
    min-height: 28px;
}

QDialog QPushButton {
    background-color: #F9A825;
    color: #3E2723;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 10px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: bold;
    padding: 8px 14px;
}

QDialog QPushButton:disabled {
    background-color: #E0D9C8;
    color: #9E9E9E;
}

QDialog QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: #E09600;
}

QDialog QLabel {
    font-size: 14px;
}
